  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#fallback-base-url\r\n\r\n> If document's [URL](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-url) is [about:blank](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#about:blank), and document's [browsing context](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-bc)'s [creator base URL](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#creator-base-url) is non-null, then return that [creator base URL](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#creator-base-url).\r\n\r\nFrom what I can tell, popups from `window.open()` will have a creator base URL.\r\n\r\nBut, if I do `window.open()` (no args) or `window.open(\"about:blank\")`, and then check the opened window in the dev console, I get:\r\n\r\n```\r\ndocument.documentURI === \"about:blank\";\r\ndocument.baseURI === \"about:blank\"; // *not* the creator base URL\r\n```\r\n\r\nAm I missing something, or is this fairly basic part of the spec wrong?",
